cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt these teaching materials, please cite this repository."
title: "An Introduction to SMT Solving"
abstract: >-
  Teaching materials for an introductory, hands-on session on satisfiability
  modulo theories (SMT) solving, aimed at first year AIMS (Autonomous
  Intelligent Machines and Systems CDT) students. The materials cover SAT and
  SMT solving with Z3 and CVC5, from propositional satisfiability and Sudoku
  through SMT-based certification, bit-vector reasoning and
  counterexample-guided inductive synthesis (CEGIS) of Lyapunov functions.
  The source code is licensed under MIT; the written teaching content is
  licensed under CC BY 4.0.
